id:                     E377
trigger_tool: cmake
phase: download|configuration|compilation
error_signature: Performing download step \(git clone\) for 'KWStyle'|KWStyle-download.*Command failed
severity: 3
category:               cmake, externalproject, offline-source, upstream-tests
match_keywords: KWStyle, ExternalProject_Add, GIT_REPOSITORY, DOWNLOAD_COMMAND, ITK_FORBID_DOWNLOADS
title: Bind test-only ExternalProject sources locally without reducing the upstream test inventory
root_cause: Enabling a project's real upstream tests may activate a test-tool ExternalProject whose build-time Git clone is unavailable on the target even though the main source is frozen.
affected_scope: CMake projects that build test tools through ExternalProject during an offline or network-restricted target build.
verification_cmd: Freeze the exact auxiliary source archive, configure ExternalProject with DOWNLOAD_COMMAND empty and an exact SOURCE_DIR, reject missing or hash-mismatched source, then run the complete upstream inventory.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: checksum-bound-local-externalproject-source
rec_description: Keep the upstream test entry enabled, fetch the fixed auxiliary revision during recipe source acquisition, and bind the extracted local directory into ExternalProject with downloads forbidden.
rec_command: Set a project-specific local source directory, enable the no-download gate, and require generated ExternalProject dirinfo to report method=source_dir with an empty command.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-source-and-cmake-externalproject-binding
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach:
fallback_description:
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern: ITK_USE_KWSTYLE.*OFF|BUILD_TESTING.*OFF|skip.*upstream.*test
forbid_1_reason: Disabling the test tool or BUILD_TESTING reduces the existing upstream inventory instead of fixing the offline source boundary.
forbid_1_consequence: A partial test run can be misreported as complete.
principles:
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
